'none'),(6676,'Unable to install the %theme theme since it requires the %required_theme theme.','','none'),(6677,'Unable to uninstall the %theme theme since the %dependent_theme theme is installed.','','none'),(6678,'Configuration %name depends on the %owner module that will not be installed after import.','','none'),(6679,'Configuration %name depends on the %owner theme that will not be installed after import.','','none'),(6680,'Configuration %name depends on the %owner extension that will not be installed after import.','','none'),(6681,'Unable to install the %module module since it requires the %required_module module.Unable to install the %module module since it requires the %required_module modules.','','none'),(6682,'Configuration %name depends on the %module module that will not be installed after import.Configuration %name depends on modules (%module) that will not be installed after import.','','none'),(6683,'Configuration %name depends on the %theme theme that will not be installed after import.Configuration %name depends on themes (%theme) that will not be installed after import.','','none'),(6684,'Configuration %name depends on the %config configuration that will not exist after import.Configuration %name depends on configuration (%config) that will not exist after import.','','none'),(6685,'Interface text','','none'),(6686,'Order of language detection methods for interface text. If a translation of interface text is available in the detected language, it will be displayed.','','none'),(6687,'Inaccessible','','none'),(6688,'NotNull','Validation','none'),(6689,'Null','Validation','none'),(6690,'Aggregator title','','none'),(6691,'Formats an aggregator item or feed title with an optional link.','','none'),(6692,'Empty block library behavior','','none'),(6693,'Provides a link to add a new block.','','none'),(6694,'Books have a hierarchical structure, called a <em>book outline</em>. Each book outline can have nested pages up to nine levels deep. Multiple content types can be configured to behave as a book outline. From the content edit form, it is possible to add a page to a book outline or create a new book.','','none'),(6695,'Configuring content types for books','','none'),(6696,'Content type for the <em>Add child page</em> link','','none'),(6697,'The configuration cannot be imported because it failed validation for the following reasons:','','none'),(6698,'Link to translate @entity_type_label','','none'),(6699,'Provide a translation link to the @entity_type_label.','','none'),(6700,'A forum is represented by a hierarchical structure, consisting of:','','none'),(6701,'<em>Forums</em> (for example, <em>Recipes for cooking vegetables</em>)','','none'),(6702,'<em>Forum topics</em> submitted by users (for example, <em>How to cook potatoes</em>), which start discussions.','','none'),(6703,'Threaded <em>comments</em> submitted by users (for example, <em>You wash the potatoes first and then...</em>).','','none'),(6704,'Optional <em>containers</em>, used to group similar forums. Forums can be placed inside containers, and vice versa.','','none'),(6705,'Setting up the forum structure','','none'),(6706,'Navigating in the forum','','none'),(6707,'Interface text language selected for page','','none'),(6708,'Customize %language_name language detection to differ from Interface text language detection settings','','none'),(6709,'The domain for %language may only contain the domain name, not a trailing slash, protocol and/or port.','','none'),(6710,'@language translation of the @type %label has been deleted.','','none'),(6711,'always_populate_raw_post_data PHP setting','','none'),(6712,'Not set to -1.','','none'),(6713,'Xdebug settings','','none'),(6714,'xdebug.max_nesting_level is set to %value.','','none'),(6715,'Set <code>xdebug.max_nesting_level=@level</code> in your PHP configuration as some pages in your Drupal site will not work when this setting is too low.','','none'),(6716,'For more detailed information, see the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/upgrade\">upgrading handbook</a>. If you are unsure what these terms mean you should probably contact your hosting provider.','','none'),(6717,'Trimmed limit','','none'),(6718,'Trimmed limit: @trim_length characters','','none'),(6719,'%name is blocked or has not been activated yet.','','none'),(6720,'Working with multilingual views','','none'),(6721,'If your site has multiple languages and translated entities, each result row in a view will contain one translation of each involved entity (a view can involve multiple entities if it uses relationships). You can use a filter to restrict your view to one language: without filtering, if an entity has three translations it will add three rows to the results; if you filter by language, at most one result will appear (it could be zero if that particular entity does not have a translation matching your language filter choice). If a view uses relationships, each entity in the relationship needs to be filtered separately. You can filter a view to a fixed language choice, such as English or Spanish, or to the language selected by the page the view is displayed on (the language that is selected for the page by the language detection settings either for Content or User interface).','','none'),(6722,'Because each result row contains a specific translation of each entity, field-level filters are also relative to these entity translations. For example, if your view has a filter that specifies that the entity title should contain a particular English word, you will presumably filter out all rows containing Chinese translations, since they will not contain the English word. If your view also has a second filter specifying that the title should contain a particular Chinese word, and if you are using \"And\" logic for filtering, you will presumably end up with no results in the view, because there are probably not any entity translations containing both the English and Chinese words in the title.','','none'),(6723,'Independent of filtering, you can choose the display language (the language used to display the entities and their fields) via a setting on the display. Your language choices are the same as the filter language choices, with an additional choice of \"Content language of view row\" and \"Original language of content in view row\", which means to display each entity in the result row using the language that entity has or in which it was originally created. In theory, this would give you the flexibility to filter to French translations, for instance, and then display the results in Spanish. The more usual choices would be to use the same language choices for the display language and each entity filter in the view, or to use the Row language setting for the display.','','none'),(6724,'Entity link','','none'),(6725,'Entity delete link','','none'),(6726,'Entity edit link','','none'),(6727,'Link to @entity_type_label','','none'),(6728,'Link to edit @entity_type_label','','none'),(6729,'Provide an edit link to the @entity_type_label.','','none'),(6730,'Link to delete @entity_type_label','','none'),(6731,'Provide a delete link to the @entity_type_label.','','none'),(6732,'View','View entity type','8.6.9'),(6733,'Options such as paging, table sorting, and exposed filters will not initiate a page refresh.','','none'),(6734,'Select pager','','none'),(6735,'This can be an internal Drupal path such as node/add or an external URL such as \"https://www.drupal.org\". You may use the \"Replacement patterns\" above.','','none'),(6736,'Per default the table is hidden for an empty view. With this option it is possible to show an empty table with the text in it.','','none'),(6737,'Cache tags','','none'),(6738,'Timestamp display format settings','','none'),(6739,'Future format','','none'),(6740,'Past format','','none'),(6741,'@requirements_message (Currently using @item version @version)','','none'),(6742,'The MyISAM storage engine is not supported.','','none'),(6743,'0 seconds','',