o the <a href=\":dblog\">log</a>.','','none'),(8938,'Note that the CAPTCHA module interacts with page caching (see <a href=\":performancesettings\">performance settings</a>). Because the challenge should be unique for each generated form, the caching of the page it appears on is prevented. Make sure that these forms do not appear on too many pages or you will lose much caching efficiency. For example, if you put a CAPTCHA on the user login block, which typically appears on each page for anonymous visitors, caching will practically be disabled. The comment submission forms are another example. In this case you should set the <em>Location of comment submission form</em> to <em>Display on separate page</em> in the comment settings of the relevant <a href=\":contenttypes\">content types</a> for better caching efficiency.','','none'),(8939,'Users with the <em>Skip CAPTCHA</em> <a href=\":perm\">permission</a> won\'t be offered a challenge. Be sure to grant this permission to the trusted users (e.g. site administrators). If you want to test a protected form, be sure to do it as a user without the <em>Skip CAPTCHA</em> permission (e.g. as anonymous user).','','none'),(8940,'The <em>settings</em> and the <em>display</em> of the link field can be configured separately. See the <a href=\"!field_ui\">Field UI help</a> for more information on how to manage fields and their display.','','none'),(8941,'Adding link text','','none'),(8942,'In the field settings you can define additional link text to be <em>optional</em> or <em>required</em> in any link field.','','none'),(8943,'Displaying link text','','none'),(8944,'If link text has been submitted for a URL, then by default this link text is displayed as a link to the URL. If you want to display both the link text <em>and</em> the URL, choose the appropriate link format from the drop-down menu in the <em>Manage display</em> page. If you only want to display the URL even if link text has been submitted, choose <em>Link</em> as the format, and then change its <em>Format settings</em> to display <em>URL only</em>.','','none'),(8945,'You can add attributes to links, by changing the <em>Format settings</em> in the <em>Manage display</em> page. Adding <em>rel=\"nofollow\"</em> notifies search engines that links should not be followed.','','none'),(8946,'All links are validated after a link field is filled in. They can include anchors or query strings.','','none'),(8947,'Quebec','','none'),(8948,'Saskatchewan','','none'),(8949,'Capture','','none'),(8950,'Applies to','','none'),(8951,'Alphanumeric','','none'),(8952,'PayPal Email','','none'),(8953,'Discover Card','','none'),(8954,'Product category','','none'),(8955,'Even if selected, this area handler will never render if a valid order cannot be found in the View\'s arguments.','','none'),(8956,'Commerce Price','','none'),(8957,'Captured','','none'),(8958,'Used by all orders of this type.','','none'),(8959,'Saved the %label order type.','','none'),(8960,'You have not created any order types yet. Go to the <a href=\"@create_order_type\">order type creation page</a> to add a new order type.','','none'),(8961,'Commerce Price requires the commerceguys/intl library.','','none'),(8962,'Fraction digits','','none'),(8963,'Default price formatter settings','','none'),(8964,'Strip trailing zeroes after the decimal point','','none'),(8965,'The number of digits after the decimal sign.','','none'),(8966,'The currency code must consist of three uppercase letters.','','none'),(8967,'The currency code is already in use.','','none'),(8968,'The numeric code must consist of three digits.','','none'),(8969,'The numeric code is already in use.','','none'),(8970,'Saved the %label currency.','','none'),(8971,'All currencies have already been imported.','','none'),(8972,'Strip trailing zeroes after the decimal point.','','none'),(8973,'The alternative URL for this product. Use a relative path. For example, \"/my-product\".','','none'),(8974,'Manage your products.','','8.6.9