e before, it will continue to return only the absolute file URL. If you want the new behavior, which returns both the stored URI and a root-relative file URL, <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/node/2925783\">read the change record to learn how to opt in.</a>','','none'),(10016,'Whether to retain pre Drupal 8.5 behavior of normalizing the File entity \"uri\" field value to an absolute URL.','','none'),(10017,'@title field is required if there is @uri input.','','none'),(10018,'The Media module manages the creation, editing, deletion, settings, and display of media. Items are typically images, documents, slideshows, YouTube videos, tweets, Instagram photos, etc. You can reference media items from any other content on your site. For more information, see the <a href=\":media\">online documentation for the Media module</a>.','','none'),(10019,'Listing media items','','none'),(10020,'Media items are listed at the <a href=\":media-collection\">media administration page</a>.','','none'),(10021,'Adding media to other content','','none'),(10022,'Users with permission to administer content types can add media support by adding a media reference field to the content type on the content type administration page. (The same is true of block types, taxonomy terms, user profiles, and other content that supports fields.) A media reference field can refer to any configured media type. It is possible to allow multiple media types in the same field.','','none'),(10023,'Differences between Media, File, and Image reference fields','','none'),(10024,'<em>Media</em> reference fields offer several advantages over basic <em>File</em> and <em>Image</em> references:','','none'),(10025,'Media reference fields can reference multiple media types in the same field.','','none'),(10026,'Fields can also be added to media types themselves, which means that custom metadata like descriptions and taxonomy tags can be added for the referenced media. (Basic file and image fields do not support this.)','','none'),(10027,'Media types for audio and video files are provided by default, so there is no need for additional configuration to upload these media.','','none'),(10028,'Contributed or custom projects can provide additional media sources (such as third-party websites, Twitter, etc.).','','none'),(10029,'Existing media items can be reused on any other content items with a media reference field.','','none'),(10030,'Use <em>Media</em> reference fields for most files, images, audio, videos, and remote media. Use <em>File</em> or <em>Image</em> reference fields when creating your own media types, or for legacy files and images created before enabling the Media module.','','none'),(10031,'For more information, see the <a href=\"@help_url\">Media help page</a>.','','none'),(10032,'%type_name: Create new media','','none'),(10033,'%type_name: Edit own media','','none'),(10034,'%type_name: Edit any media','','none'),(10035,'%type_name: Delete own media','','none'),(10036,'<em>The media source cannot be changed after the media type is created.</em>','','none'),(10037,'Use audio files for reusable media.','','none'),(10038,'Use video files for reusable media.','','none'),(10039,'The destination system contains data which was not created by a migration.','','none'),(10040,'Migrate Drupal settings','','none'),(10041,'source_module enforcement tags','','none'),(10042,'Upgrade a site by importing its files and the data from its database into a clean and empty new install of Drupal 8. See the <a href=\":url\">Drupal site upgrades handbook</a> for more information.','','none'),(10043,'Old site','','none'),(10044,'New site','','none'),(10045,'This empty Drupal 8 installation you will import the old site to.','','none'),(10046,'Preparation steps','','none'),(10047,'WARNING: Content may be overwritten on your new site.','','none'),(10048,'I acknowledge I may lose data. Continue anyway.','','none'),(10049,'There is conflicting content of these types:','','none'),(10050,'It looks like you have content on your new site which <strong>may be overwritten</strong> if you continue to run this upgrade. The upgrade should be performed on a clean Drupal 8 installation. For more information see the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":id-conflicts-handbook\">upgrade handbook</a>.','','none'),(10051,'There is translated content of these types:','','none'),(10052,'It looks like you are migrating translated content from your old site. Possible ID conflicts for translations are not automatically detected in the current version of Drupal. Refer to the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":id-conflicts-handbook\">upgrade handbook</a> for instructions on how to avoid ID conflicts with translated content.','','none'),(10053,'On the <a href=\":cache-settings\">Performance page</a>, you can configure how long browsers and proxies may cache pages based on the Cache-Control header; this setting is ignored by the Internal Page Cache module, which caches pages permanently until invalidation, unless they carry an Expires header. There is no other configuration.','','none'),(10054,'Either the path \'@link_path\' is invalid or you do not have access to it.','','none'),(10055,'The Settings Tray module allows users with the <a href=\":administer_block_permission\">Administer blocks</a> and <a href=\":contextual_permission\">Use contextual links</a> permissions to edit blocks without visiting a separate page. For more information, see the <a href=\":handbook_url\">online documentation for the Settings Tray module</a>.','','none'),(10056,'Editing blocks in place','','none'),(10057,'To edit blocks in place, either click the <strong>Edit</strong> button in the toolbar and then click on the block, or choose \"Quick edit\" from the block\'s contextual link. (See the <a href=\":contextual\">Contextual Links module help</a> for more information about how to use contextual links.)','','none'),(10058,'The Settings Tray for the block will open in a sidebar, with a compact form for configuring what the block shows.','','none'),(10059,'Save the form and the changes will be immediately visible on the page.','','none'),(10060,'Provides a sidebar to configure blocks on the page.','','none'),(10061,'The ID of the node to which these statistics apply.','','none'),(10062,'Specify the format of the syslog entry. Available variables are: <dl><dt><code>!base_url</code></dt><dd>Base URL of the site.</dd><dt><code>!timestamp</code></dt><dd>Unix timestamp of the log entry.</dd><dt><code>!type</code></dt><dd>The category to which this message belongs.</dd><dt><code>!ip</code></dt><dd>IP address of the user triggering the message.</dd><dt><code>!request_uri</code></dt><dd>The requested URI.</dd><dt><code>!referer</code></dt><dd>HTTP Referer if available.</dd><dt><code>!severity</code></dt><dd>The severity level of the event; ranges from 0 (Emergency) to 7 (Debug).</dd><dt><code>!uid</code></dt><dd>User ID.</dd><dt><code>!link</code></dt><dd>A link to associate with the message.</dd><dt><code>!message</code></dt><dd>The message to store in the log.</dd></dl>','','none'),(10063,'Either the path \'%path\' is invalid or you do not have access to it.','','none'),(10064,'%capital_name contains the following terms.','','none'),(10065,'%capital_name contains terms grouped under parent terms','','none'),(10066,'%capital_name contains terms with multiple parents.','','none'),(10067,'%vocabulary: Create terms','','none'),(10068,'%vocabulary: Edit terms','','none'),(10069,'Output the URL as text','','none'),(10070,'Output an absolute link','','none'),(10071,'Min placeholder','','none'),(10072,'Max placeholder','','none'),(10073,'Enable this option to output an absolute link. Required if you want to use the path as a link destination.','','none'),(10074,'Enforce a <code>destination</code> parameter in the link to return the user to the original view upon completing the link action. Most operations include a destination by default and this setting is no longer needed.','','none'),(10075,'Hint text that appears inside the Min field when empty.','','none'),(10076,'Hint text that appears inside the Max field when empty.','','none'),(10077,'Hint text that appears inside the field when empty.','','none'),(10078,'There are no workflow types available. In order to create workflows you need to install a module that provides a workflow type. For example, the <a href=\":content-moderation\">Content Moderation</a> module provides a workflow type that enables workflows for content entities.','','none'),(10079,'Transition label','','none'),(10080,'Find and moderate content.','','none'),(10081,'No moderated content available. Only pending versions of content, such as drafts, are listed here.','','none'),(10082,'Workspace name','','none'),(10083,'A flag indicating whether this was a default revision when it was saved.','','none'),(10084,'The Content Moderation module allows you to expand on Drupal\'s \"unpublished\" and \"published\" states for content. It allows you to have a published version that is live, but have a separate working copy that is undergoing review before it is published. This is achieved by using <a href=\":workflows\">Workflows</a> to apply different states and transitions to entities as needed. For more information, see the <a href=\":content_moderation\">online documentation for the Content Moderation module</a>.','','none'),(10085,'Applying workflows','','none'),(10086,'Content Moderation allows you to apply <a href=\":workflows\">Workflows</a> to content, custom blocks, and other <a href=\":field_help\" title=\"Field module help, with background on content entities\">content entities</a>, to provide more fine-grained publishing options. For example, a Basic page might have states such as Draft and Published, with allowed transitions such as Draft to Published (making the current revision \"live\"), and Published to Draft (making a new draft revision of published content).','','none'),(10087,'You can view a list of content awaiting moderation on the <a href=\":moderated\">moderated content page</a>. This will show any content in an unpublished state, such as Draft or Archived, to help surface content that requires more work from content editors.','','none'),(10088,'Each transition is exposed as a permission. If a user has the permission for a transition, they can use the transition to change the state of the content item, from Draft to Published.','','none'),(10089,'Provides moderation states for content.','','none'),(10090,'Content translation bundle settings','','none'),(10091,'Fields that apply to all languages are hidden to avoid conflicting changes. <a href=\":url\">Edit them on the original language form</a>.','','none'),(10092,'Content translation synchronized fields','Validation','none'),(10093,'Non-translatable field elements can only be changed when updating the original language.','','none'),(10094,'The node language.','','none'),(10095,'This layout builder tool allows you to configure the layout of the main content area.','','none'),(10096,'To manage other areas of the page, use the <a href=\"@block-ui\">block administration page</a>.','','none'),(10097,'To manage other areas of the page, use the block administration page.','','none'),(10098,'Layout Builder provides layout building utility.','','none'),(10099,'For more information, see the <a href=\":layout-builder-documentation\">online documentation for the Layout Builder module</a>.','','none'),(10100,'Provides layout building utility.','','none'),(10101,'Configure any layout','','none'),(10102,'Configure section','','none'),(10103,'Per-view-mode Layout Builder settings','','none'),(10104,'Allow a customized layout','','none'),(10105,'Layout section','','none'),(10106,'Edit layout for %label','','none'),(10107,'The layout override has been saved.','','none'),(10108,'The changes to the layout have been discarded.','','none'),(10109,'@entity being viewed','','none'),(10110,'@bundle @label','','none'),(10111,'Allow each @entity to have its layout c