t of top-level domains is required if <em>Multiple top-level domains</em> has been selected.','','none'),(10536,'Debugging enabled','','none'),(10537,'Track downloads','','none'),(10538,'Enter PHP code in the field for tracking visibility settings.','','none'),(10539,'Mailto links','','none'),(10540,'AdSense ads','','none'),(10541,'Anonymize IP','','none'),(10542,'Search and Advertising','','none'),(10543,'URL fragments','','none'),(10544,'Track User ID','','none'),(10545,'Track enhanced link attribution','','none'),(10546,'Track changing URL fragments as pageviews','','none'),(10547,'By default, the URL reported to Google Analytics will not include the \"fragment identifier\" (i.e. the portion of the URL beginning with a hash sign), and hash changes by themselves will not cause new pageviews to be reported. Checking this box will cause hash changes to be reported as pageviews (in modern browsers) and all pageview URLs to include the fragment where applicable.','','none'),(10548,'Track display features','','none'),(10549,'Custom dimensions','','none'),(10550,'Index number','','none'),(10551,'Custom dimension index #@index','','none'),(10552,'The custom dimension value.','','none'),(10553,'Custom dimension value #@index','','none'),(10554,'Custom metrics','','none'),(10555,'Custom metric index #@index','','none'),(10556,'The custom metric value.','','none'),(10557,'Custom metric value #@index','','none'),(10558,'Create only fields','','none'),(10559,'Code in this textarea will be added <strong>before</strong> <code>ga(\"send\", \"pageview\");</code>.','','none'),(10560,'Code in this textarea will be added <strong>after</strong> <code>ga(\"send\", \"pageview\");</code>. This is useful if you\'d like to track a site in two accounts.','','none'),(10561,'If checked, the Google Universal Analytics debugging script will be loaded. You should not enable your production site to use this version of the JavaScript. The analytics_debug.js script is larger than the analytics.js tracking code and it is not typically cached. Using it in your production site will slow down your site for all of your users. Again, this is only for your own testing purposes. Debug messages are printed to the <code>window.console</code> object.','','none'),(10562,'List of download file extensions cannot empty.','','none'),(10563,'The %element-title field contains invalid input.','','none'),(10564,'Display features','','none'),(10565,'Create only field name %name is a disallowed field name. Changing the <em>Tracker Name</em> is currently not supported.','','none'),(10566,'Create only field name %name is a disallowed field name. Please select <em>Multiple top-level domains</em> under <em>What are you tracking</em> to enable cross domain tracking.','','none'),(10567,'A create only field requires a value.','','none'),(10568,'The value of a create only field must be a string at most 255 characters long.','','none'),(10569,'Pages by their paths','','none'),(10570,'Path \"@page\" not prefixed with slash.','','none'),(10571,'File extension list','','none'),(10572,'Custom code snippets','','none'),(10573,'User ID enables the analysis of groups of sessions, across devices, using a unique, persistent, and non-personally identifiable ID string representing a user. <a href=\":url\">Learn more about the benefits of using User ID</a>.','','none'),(10574,'A file extension list separated by the | character that will be tracked as download when clicked. Regular expressions are supported. For example: @extensions','','none'),(10575,'@module (<span class=\"admin-missing\">disabled</span>)','','none'),(10576,'<a href=\":ga_url\">Google Analytics</a> is a free (registration required) website traffic and marketing effectiveness service.','','none'),(10577,'Google Analytics module has not been configured yet. Please configure its settings from the <a href=\":url\">Google Analytics settings page</a>.','','none'),(10578,'Google Analytics module has debugging enabled. Please disable debugging setting in production sites from the <a href=\":url\">Google Analytics settings page</a>.','','none'),(10579,'Track content in colorbox modal dialogs','','none'),(10580,'Enable enhanced link attribution','','none'),(10581,'Load debugging code of Google Universal Analytics','','none'),(10582,'Link attribution','','none'),(10583,'This ID is unique to each site you want to track separately, and is in the form of UA-xxxxxxx-yy. To get a Web Property ID, <a href=\":analytics\">register your site with Google Analytics</a>, or if you already have registered your site, go to your Google Analytics Settings page to see the ID next to every site profile. <a href=\":webpropertyid\">Find more information in the documentation</a>.','','none'),(10584,'If you selected \"Multiple top-level domains\" above, enter all related top-level domains. Add one domain per line. By default, the data in your reports only includes the path and name of the page, and not the domain name. For more information see section <em>Show separate domain names</em> in <a href=\":url\">Tracking Multiple Domains</a>.','','none'),(10585,'Enable to track the content shown in colorbox modal windows.','','none'),(10586,'Enhanced Link Attribution improves the accuracy of your In-Page Analytics report by automatically differentiating between multiple links to the same URL on a single page by using link element IDs. <a href=\":url\">Enable enhanced link attribution</a> in the Admin UI of your Google Analytics account.','','none'),(10587,'If checked, internal search keywords are tracked. You must configure your Google account to use the internal query parameter <strong>search</strong>. For more information see <a href=\":url\">Setting Up Site Search for a Profile</a>.','','none'),(10588,'The display features plugin can be used to enable Display Advertising Features in Google Analytics, such as Remarketing, Demographics and Interest Reporting, and more. <a href=\":displayfeatures\">Learn more about Display Advertising Features in Google Analytics</a>. If you choose this option you will need to <a href=\":privacy\">update your privacy policy</a>.','','none'),(10589,'You can set values for Google Analytics <a href=\":custom_var_documentation\">Custom Dimensions</a> here. You must have already configured your custom dimensions in the <a href=\":setup_documentation\">Google Analytics Management Interface</a>. You may use tokens. Global and user tokens are always available; on node pages, node tokens are also available. A dimension <em>value</em> is allowed to have a maximum length of 150 bytes. Expect longer values to get trimmed.','','none'),(10590,'You can supplement Google Analytics\' basic IP address tracking of visitors by segmenting users based on custom dimensions. Section 7 of the <a href=\":ga_tos\">Google Analytics terms of service</a> requires that You will not (and will not allow any third party to) use the Service to track, collect or upload any data that personally identifies an individual (such as a name, userid, email address or billing information), or other data which can be reasonably linked to such information by Google. You will have and abide by an appropriate Privacy Policy and will comply with all applicable laws and regulations relating to the collection of information from Visitors. You must post a Privacy Policy and that Privacy Policy must provide notice of Your use of cookies that are used to collect traffic data, and You must not circumvent any privacy features (e.g., an opt-out) that are part of the Service.','','none'),(10591,'You can add Google Analytics <a href=\":custom_var_documentation\">Custom Metrics</a> here. You must have already configured your custom metrics in the <a href=\":setup_documentation\">Google Analytics Management Interface</a>. You may use tokens. Global and user tokens are always available; on node pages, node tokens are also available.','','none'),(10592,'You can supplement Google Analytics\' basic IP address tracking of visitors by segmenting users based on custom metrics. Section 7 of the <a href=\":ga_tos\">Google Analytics terms of service</a> requires that You will not (and will not allow any third party to) use the Service to track, collect or upload any data that personally identifies an individual (such as a name, userid, email address or billing information), or other data which can be reasonably linked to such information by Google. You will have and abide by an appropriate Privacy Policy and will comply with all applicable laws and regulations relating to the collection of information from Visitors. You must post a Privacy Policy and that Privacy Policy must provide notice of Your use of cookies that are used to collect traffic data, and You must not circumvent any privacy features (e.g., an opt-out) that are part of the Service.','','none'),(10593,'You can add custom Google Analytics <a href=\":snippets\">code snippets</a> here. These will be added every time tracking is in effect. Before you add your custom code, you should read the <a href=\":ga_concepts_overview\">Google Analytics Tracking Code - Functional Overview</a> and the <a href=\":ga_js_api\">Google Analytics Tracking API</a> documentation. <strong>Do not include the &lt;script&gt; tags</strong>, and always end your code with a semicolon (;).','','none'),(10594,'Enter one value per line, in the format name|value. Settings in this textarea will be added to <code>ga(\"create\", \"UA-XXXX-Y\", {\"name\":\"value\"});</code>. For more information, read <a href=\":url\">create only fields</a> documentation in the Analytics.js field reference.','','none'),(10595,'Create only field name %name is an unknown field name. Field names are case sensitive. Please see <a href=\":url\">create only fields</a> documentation for supported field names.','','none'),(10596,'This will track the selected message types shown to users. Tracking of form validation errors may help you identifying usability issues in your site. For each visit (user session), a maximum of approximately 500 combined GATC requests (both events and page views) can be tracked. Every message is tracked as one individual event. Note that - as the number of events in a session approaches the limit - additional events might not be tracked. Messages from excluded pages cannot be tracked.','','none'),(10597,'Add JavaScript snippets','','none'),(10598,'Google Analytics adds a web statistics tracking system to your website. This system incorporates numerous statistical features. For an extensive listing of these features see the <a href=\":project\">Google Analytics</a> project site. Beyond that, additional information can be found at the <a href=\":documentation\">Drupal - Google Analytics documentation</a>.','','none'),(10599,'Configuring Google Analytics','','none'),(10600,'All settings for this module can be found on the <a href=\":ga_settings\">Google Analytics settings</a> page. When entering the Google Analytics account number here, it will automatically add the required JavaScript to every page generated. The <em>General Settings</em> section on this page provides additional instruction about setting up tracking thru the Google account.','','none'),(10601,'Additional features','','none'),(10602,'The Google Analytics module offers a bit more than basic tracking. <em>Page Tracking</em> for instance allows you to provide a list of pages to track, or a list of pages not to track. Role and Link tracking features are also available. For a comprehensive discussion on the setup and use of its many feature see the <a href=\":documentation\">Drupal - Google Analytics documentation</a>.','','none'),(10603,'Enter JavaScript code snippets for advanced Google Analytics functionality.','','none'),(10604,'Premium account','','none'),(10605,'If you are a Google Analytics Premium customer, you can use up to 200 instead of 20 custom dimensions and metrics.','','none'),(10606,'Transparency','','none'),(10607,'Frameborder','','none'),(10608,'Scrolling','','none'),(10609,'The <em>settings</em> and the <em>display</em> of the iframe field can be configured separately. See the <a href=\":field_ui\">Field UI help</a> for more information on how to manage fields and their display.','','none'),(10610,'Provides a widget for inline management (creation, modification, removal) of referenced entities. ','','none'),(10611,'You have added @entities_count out of @cardinality_count allowed @label.','','none'),(10612,'Are you sure you want to remove %label?','','none'),(10613,'Allow users to add new @label.','','none'),(10614,'Match operator','','none'),(10615,'Label (singular)','','none'),(10616,'Label (plural)','','none'),(10617,'Default labels are used.','','none'),(10618,'Are you sure you want to remove this %entity_type?','','none'),(10619,'Allow new','','none'),(10620,'Allow existing','','none'),(10621,'@entity_type entities','','none'),(10622,'Form mode: @mode','','none'),(10623,'Remove \"Home\" link','','none'),(10624,'Show current page as link','','none'),(10625,'Add \"Home\" link','','none'),(10626,'Use site name instead of \"Home\" link','','none'),(10627,'There are no menus yet.','','none'),(10628,'Paragraph','','none'),(10629,'Add mode','','none'),(10630,'Paragraphs','','none'),(10631,'The array values each cleaned by Pathauto and then joined with the slash into a string that resembles an URL.','','none'),(10632,'Selection criteria','','none'),(10633,'Bulk generate','','none'),(10634,'Selection logic','','none'),(10635,'Pattern type','','none'),(10636,'Delete options','','none'),(10637,'All of your %label path aliases have been deleted.','','none'),(10638,'See <a href=\":pathauto-help\">Pathauto help</a> for details.','','none'),(10639,'Maximum length of aliases to generate. 100 is the recommended length. @max is the maximum possible length.','','none'),(10640,'Maximum text length of any component in the alias (e.g., [title]). 100 is the recommended length. @max is the maximum possible length.','','none'),(10641,'The <a href=\":url\">Redirect module settings</a> affect whether a redirect is created when an alias is deleted.','','none'),(10642,'Considering installing the <a href=\":url\">Redirect module</a> to get redirects when your aliases change.','','none'),(10643,'Selection condition','','none'),(10644,'Entity of type @type was not processed. It defines the following patterns: @patterns','','none'),(10645,'Unrecognized entity bundle @entity:@bundle was not processed. It defines the following patterns: @patterns','','none'),(10646,'Add Pathauto pattern','','none'),(10647,'Pathauto pattern config','','none'),(10648,'Pathauto state','','none'),(10649,'Whether an automated alias should be created or not.','','none'),(10650,'Pathauto pattern','','8.6.9'),(10651,'Check to which types this pattern should be applied. Leave empty to allow any.','','none'),(10652,'Check to which languages this pattern should be applied. Leave empty to allow any.','','none'),(10653,'@label being aliased','','none'),(10654,'Updated alias for %label @id.','','none'),(10655,'Updated 1 %label URL alias.Updated @count %label URL aliases.','','none'),(10656,'When a pattern includes certain characters (such as those with accents) should Pathauto attempt to transliterate them into the US-ASCII alphabet?','','none'),(10657,'This page provides a list of all patterns on the site and allows you to edit and reorder them.','','none'),(10658,'The %element-title is using the following invalid characters: @invalid-characters.','','none'),(10659,'Convert token values to lowercase.','','none'),(10660,'Are you sure you want to disable the pattern %label?','','none'),(10661,'Disabled patterns are ignored when generating aliases.','','none'),(10662,'Disabled pattern %label.','','none'),(10663,'Are you sure you want to enable the pattern %label?','','none'),(10664,'Enabled pattern %label.','','none'),(10665,'Update URL alias of an entity','','none'),(10666,'The Pathauto module provides a mechanism to automate the creation of <a href=\"path\">path</a> aliases. This makes URLs more readable and helps search engines index content more effectively.  For more information, see the <a href=\":online\">online documentation for Pathauto</a>.','','none'),(10667,'Pathauto is accessed from the tabs it adds to the list of <a href=\":aliases\">URL aliases</a>.','','none'),(10668,'Creating Pathauto Patterns','','none'),(10669,'The <a href=\":pathauto_pattern\">\"Patterns\"</a> page is used to configure automatic path aliasing.  New patterns are created here using the <a href=\":add_form\">Add Pathauto pattern</a> button which presents a form to simplify pattern creation thru the use of <a href=\"token\">available tokens</a>. The patterns page provides a list of all patterns on the site and allows you to edit and reorder them. An alias is generated for the first pattern that applies.','','none'),(10670,'The <a href=\":settings\">\"Settings\"</a> page is used to customize global Pathauto settings for automated pattern creation.','','none'),(10671,'The <strong>maximum alias length</strong> and <strong>maximum component length</strong> values default to 100 and have a limit of @max from Pathauto. You should enter a value that is the length of the \"alias\" column of the url_alias database table minus the length of any strings that might get added to the end of the URL. The recommended and default value is 100.','','none'),(10672,'Bulk Generation','','none'),(10673,'The <a href=\":pathauto_bulk\">\"Bulk Generate\"</a> page allows you to create URL aliases for items that currently have no aliases. This is typically used when installing Pathauto on a site that has existing un-aliased content that needs to be aliased in bulk.','','none'),(10674,'Delete Aliases','','none'),(10675,'The <a href=\":pathauto_delete\">\"Delete Aliases\"</a> page allows you to remove URL aliases from items that have previously been assigned aliases using pathauto.','','none'),(10676,'You need to select a pattern type, then a pattern and filter, and a label. Additional types can be enabled on the <a href=\":settings\">Settings</a> page.','','none'),(10677,'Enabled entity types','','none'),(10678,'Enable to add a path field and allow to define alias patterns for the given type. Disabled types already define a path field themselves or currently have a pattern.','','none'),(10679,'Broken type','','none'),(10680,'AliasType','','none'),(10681,'Bulk generation can be used to generate URL aliases for items that currently have no aliases. This is typically used when installing Pathauto on a site that has existing un-aliased content that needs to be aliased in bulk.','','none'),(10682,'It can also be used to regenerate URL aliases for items that have an old alias and for which the Pathauto pattern has been changed.','','none'),(10683,'Note that this will only affect items which are configured to have their URL alias automatically set. Items whose URL alias is manually set are not affected.','','none'),(10684,'The %element-title doesn\'t allow the patterns ending with whitespace.','','none'),(10685,'Select the types of paths for which to generate URL aliases','','none'),(10686,'Select which URL aliases to generate','','none'),(10687,'Generate a URL alias for un-aliased paths only','','none'),(10688,'<a href=\":url\">Pathauto settings</a> are set to ignore paths which already have a URL alias. You can only create URL aliases for paths having none.','','none'),(10689,'Update the URL alias for paths having an old URL alias','','none'),(10690,'Regenerate URL aliases for all paths','','none'),(10691,'A short name to help you identify this pattern in the patterns list.','','none'),(10692,'Only delete automatically generated aliases','','none'),(10693,'When checked, aliases which have been manually set are not affected by this mass-deletion.','','none'),(10694,'Bulk deleting URL aliases','','none'),(10695,'All of your automatically generated path aliases have been deleted.','','none'),(10696,'All of your automatically generated %label path aliases have been deleted.','','none'),(10697,'%type is used by 1 profile on your site. You can not remove this profile type until you have removed all of the %type profiles.%type is used by @count profiles on your site. You may not remove %type until you have removed all of the %type profiles.','','none'),(10698,'State Machine','','none'),(10699,'@type field. Also known as %labels.','','none'),(10700,'Tokens or token types not defined as arrays','','none'),(10701,'Tokens or token types missing name property','','none'),(10702,'Token types do not have any tokens defined','','none'),(10703,'Token types are not defined but have tokens','','none'),(10704,'Token or token types are defined by multiple modules','','none'),(10705,'The URI to the image.','','none'),(10706,'The URL to the image.','','none'),(10707,'@label tokens.','','none'),(10708,'@type type with delta @delta','','none'),(10709,'The <a href=\":project\">Token</a> module provides a user interface for the site token system. It also adds some additional tokens that are used extensively during site development. Tokens are specially formatted chunks of text that serve as placeholders for a dynamically generated value. For more information, covering both the token system and the additional tools provided by the Token module, see the <a href=\":online\">online documentation</a>.','','none'),(10710,'Your website uses a shared token system for exposing and using placeholder tokens and their appropriate replacement values. This allows for any module to provide placeholder tokens for strings without having to reinvent the wheel. It also ensures consistency in the syntax used for tokens, making the system as a whole easier for end users to use.','','none'),(10711,'The list of the currently available tokens on this site are shown below.','','none'),(10712,'%name is using the following invalid tokens: @invalid-tokens.','','none'),(10713,'Computed menu link for the node (only a